  "label" : "Advisor Quote / Bio",
  "required" : false,
  "locked" : false,
  "type" : "richtext",
  "display_width" : null,
  "default" : "<p>The question isn't whether AI can generate content — it can. The real question is whether that content constitutes thought leadership. Spoiler: it doesn't. Thought leadership requires judgment, humility, and a point of view shaped by lived experience. Things AI cannot replicate.</p><p>In this article, MDCo's Christina Nordquist Jacobs draws on her master's research in AI and communications to explain exactly how custom GPTs can be trained on a leader's writing samples, personality profile, and communication patterns — not to generate a generic voice, but to codify and protect an authentic one.</p><p>The result is what she calls a digital fingerprint of thought leadership — and it's the foundation everything in Voice Intelligence is built on.</p>"
